		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>J&#039;ai ensuite promu mon esclave en maître : pg_ctl promote.</p><p>Dans les logs, j&#039;ai les messages :<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:24 CEST [7513]: [30-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; received promote request<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:24 CEST [7513]: [31-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; redo done at 0/F3000098<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:24 CEST [7513]: [32-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; last completed transaction was at log time 2016-05-20 10:54:51.834983+02<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:24 CEST [7513]: [33-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; restored log file &quot;0000000100000000000000F3&quot; from archive<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; cp: impossible d&#039;Ã©valuer Â«Â /home/postgres/PG_ARC/00000002.historyÂ Â»: Aucun fichier ou dossier de ce type<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:25 CEST [7513]: [34-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; selected new timeline ID: 2<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; cp: impossible d&#039;Ã©valuer Â«Â /home/postgres/PG_ARC/00000001.historyÂ Â»: Aucun fichier ou dossier de ce type<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:26 CEST [7513]: [35-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; archive recovery complete<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:26 CEST [7513]: [36-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; MultiXact member wraparound protections are now enabled<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:26 CEST [7516]: [13-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:50 CEST LOG:&#160; checkpoint starting: force<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2016-05-20 11:28:26 CEST [7511]: [3-1] user=&#160; 2016-05-20 10:54:48 CEST LOG:&#160; database system is ready to accept connections</p><br /><p>Pourquoi ces messages sur des fichiers history ?<br />Y-a-t&#039;il un nouveau problème ?</p>]]></content>
